layout "layout.faqir"

block content
  p
    | When Claude works alone for an hour, the instruction you gave it at the start is all it has. The
    strong Composer
    | helps you write that instruction well: you fill in a few fields, it builds a complete prompt from a proven template,
    | warns you about what is missing, and keeps your prompts in a library so the good ones can be reused and launched
    | again.
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="composer-desktop.png" alt="The Composer: Spec-ify, Template and Task sections on the left; the Preview with a lint warning and the rendered prompt on the right." caption="The Composer. Fill in the left side; the right side shows the finished prompt and any warnings.")
  p
    | On a computer the form and the preview sit side by side. On a phone, switch between them with
    strong Edit
    | and
    strong Preview
    | (the preview tab shows the number of warnings, such as
    code Preview (2 ⚠)
    | ).

  h2#harness The harness prompt
  p
    | The built-in template is called
    strong harness
    | . It starts with a short
    strong Task
    | section of fields that you fill in, followed by fixed guidance Claude follows on every run: how to work, when to use
    | subagents, how to check its work visually, how to use git, what to do when you are away, guardrails, and how to keep
    | a
    code PROGRESS.md
    | file with Done, Decisions, Tried and failed, Git and Next sections. That file is what you see in a session's
    a(href="/docs/sessions#side-panels") Progress panel
    | .
  p
    | The template is the file
    code harness-prompt.md
    | on the server. Editing that file updates the Composer within a few seconds; no restart needed.

  h2#fields The fields
  p None of the fields is strictly required, but the better you fill them in, the better an unattended run goes.
  dl
    dt
      strong Goal
    dd
      | What you want, in one or two sentences. Be concrete: "Add CSV export to the reports page" beats "improve
      | reports".
    dt
      strong Done when
    dd
      | A list of checks that prove the work is finished, one per row. Press Enter for a new row; Backspace on an empty
      | row removes it; pasting a list splits it into rows. The best checks are commands Claude can run, written in
      | backticks, for example
      code `npm test` passes
      | or
      code `curl localhost:3000/health` returns 200
      | . These same commands can later be re-run by Buildyboy to
      a(href="/docs/jobs#verify") verify the job
      | .
    dt
      strong Scope
    dd Files or folders Claude may change. Everything else should be treated as read-only.
    dt
      strong Limit
    dd
      | How long to keep going, for example "4 hours" or "30 iterations". This is an instruction to Claude; to enforce a
      | hard limit, set
      strong Limit (minutes)
      | when you
      a(href="/docs/jobs#launch") launch the job
      | .
    dt
      strong Subagents
    dd How many helper agents Claude may run in parallel. Default 5; 0 to work alone.
    dt
      strong Branch
    dd
      strong new
      | (with an optional name such as
      code feat/csv-export
      | ) to work on a fresh branch, or
      strong current
      | to stay on the branch that is checked out.
    dt
      strong PR
    dd Whether to open a pull request at the end. Needs Branch set to new.
    dt
      strong Unattended
    dd
      | Yes tells Claude nobody will answer questions, so it should pick safe defaults and write them down under Decisions.
      | It does not switch walk mode on by itself.

  h2#warnings Warnings
  p
    | The preview lists problems as you type, each starting with ⚠. They are advice, not errors: you can still save and
    | launch.
  dl
    dt "Done when is empty."
    dd Add at least one check, so Claude knows when to stop.
    dt "Done when has no runnable command."
    dd
      | None of the checks looks like something Claude can run. Add one in backticks, such as
      code `npm test` passes
      | .
    dt "Unattended: yes without a Limit."
    dd An unattended run with no limit may never end. Add a time or iteration limit.
    dt "PR: yes needs a new branch."
    dd Set Branch to new.
    dt "Subagents must be a whole number."
    dd Type a number such as 0, 3 or 5.
    dt "Leftover placeholder(s) in the prompt"
    dd
      | You typed something in angle brackets, like
      code <file name>
      | , that looks like an unfilled blank. Replace it with the real value (text in backticks is ignored).

  h2#preview Preview and output
  p
    | The preview has two tabs:
    strong Rendered
    | , easy to read, and
    strong Raw Markdown
    | , exactly what Claude will receive. Under it,
    strong Use it
    | offers three ways to use the prompt:
  ul
    li
      strong Launch as a job
      | : saves the prompt (if it changed) and opens the job form with it selected. This is the usual way; see
      a(href="/docs/jobs#launch") Jobs
      | .
    li
      strong Copy Markdown
      | or
      strong Download TASK.md
      | : take the prompt elsewhere.
    li
      | Ready-made
      strong Bash
      | and
      strong PowerShell
      | commands that run the downloaded
      code TASK.md
      | with
      code claude -p
      | by hand, using the
      strong Permission mode
      | and
      strong Max budget (USD)
      | chosen just above them.
  +callout(variant="muted")
    @content
      p
        | The Permission mode and Max budget next to the copy buttons only change those copy-and-paste commands. A job
        | launched with
        strong Launch as a job
        | takes its own settings from the job form.

  h2#spec Attaching a spec
  p
    | For bigger tasks, give Claude a specification. Under
    strong Attach spec
    | choose one of:
  ul
    li
      strong Paste markdown
      | : paste the text, or use
      strong Load from a .md file
      | . It is added at the end of the prompt under a "Spec" heading.
    li
      strong File in the repo
      | : type a path such as
      code docs/spec.md
      | . The prompt then just tells Claude to read that file before starting.
  p Only the tab you have selected is used.

  h2#spec-ify Spec-ify: from a rough idea to a draft
  p
    strong Spec-ify (optional)
    | turns a one-line idea into a Goal, a Done when list, a Scope and a draft spec. Type the idea, for example "add
    | CSV export to the reports page, streaming, with a test for 1M rows", pick a
    strong Machine
    | and a
    strong Repository
    | , and press
    strong Spec-ify
    | .
  p
    | Behind the scenes this starts a real job on that machine: an Opus run with a $1 budget that reads the repository
    | and drafts the fields. It needs the machine's
    a(href="/docs/runner") runner
    | to be online, and it appears in your Jobs list as "Spec-ify: …". When it finishes, the Composer fills in Goal, Done
    | when, Scope and the spec ("Spec-ify filled Goal, Done when, Scope and the spec. Review them, then save.").
  +callout(variant="warning")
    @content
      p
        | Spec-ify
        strong replaces
        | whatever was in those fields, and only fills them in while the Composer stays open. If you navigate away, the
        | draft is still in the job's result on its job page, but you will have to copy it over yourself. Nothing is saved
        | until you save.

  h2#library Saving and the library
  p
    | Give the prompt a
    strong Title
    | (it defaults to the start of the Goal) and optional
    strong Tags
    | (comma separated, for example "backend, nightly"), then press
    strong Save to library
    | .
  ul
    li
      strong Save new version
      | stores the current state as the next version (
      code v2
      | ,
      code v3
      | …). Every save makes a version, even without changes.
    li
      strong Save as new prompt
      | makes an independent copy.
    li
      strong History
      | compares any two versions as a diff (choose
      strong From
      | and
      strong To
      | ) and can load an old version into the editor with
      strong Load vN into the editor
      | . Loading changes nothing until you save.
  p
    | The
    strong Library
    | tab lists all saved prompts with a search box and tag filters. Each card shows the version, the template, and how
    | the prompt has performed as a job: number of runs, success rate, average cost and average duration. Its buttons are
    strong Open
    | ,
    strong Duplicate
    | ,
    strong History
    | and
    strong Delete
    | (press
    strong Confirm delete
    | to really delete).
  p
    | Start over at any time with
    strong New prompt
    | at the top.

  h2#templates Your own templates
  p
    | Besides the harness, you can add templates of your own, for example a short bug-fix prompt. Under
    strong Template
    | press
    strong + Add template
    | , give it a
    strong Template name
    | , and paste or upload the Markdown (.md, .markdown or .txt). Every
    code <placeholder>
    | in it becomes a field in the Composer. Then press
    strong Add template
    | .
  ul
    li Adding a template with an existing name replaces it.
    li The name harness is reserved; to change the built-in template, edit harness-prompt.md on the server.
    li
      | A template with no
      code <placeholder>
      | is refused.
    li
      strong Remove
      | deletes an uploaded template, unless saved prompts still use it.
  p Spec-ify fills the Goal, Done when and Scope fields, so it is meant for the harness template.

  h2#tips Tips for prompts that work unattended
  ul
    li Give one goal per prompt. Two unrelated goals make it hard to say when it is done.
    li
      | Make every Done when check runnable and observable:
      code `npm test` passes
      | is checkable; "the code is clean" is not.
    li Keep Scope tight. A small scope keeps the diff reviewable.
    li Always pair Unattended with a Limit, and set a budget on the job.
    li Read the Raw Markdown once before launching. It is exactly what Claude will read.
